  "nl_text": "The rschema_0047 database is designed to manage information about news articles, their reporters, editors, and publishers. The Reporter table stores details about individual reporters, including their email, phone number, unique Reporter ID, and name. The News_Article table contains information about each article, such as its content, title, publication time, review time, and submission time, with a unique Article ID serving as its primary key. The Editor table holds data about editors, including their email, phone number, and unique Editor ID. Similarly, the Publisher table stores information about publishers, including their email, phone number, and unique Publisher ID. The Article_Reporter_Table, Article_Editor_Table, and Article_Publisher_Table are bridge tables that establish relationships between news articles and the entities involved in their creation and publication, with each table having a composite primary key consisting of the Article ID and the ID of the respective entity. The Article_Reporter_Table links articles to their respective reporters, the Article_Editor_Table links articles to their editors, and the Article_Publisher_Table links articles to their publishers, with foreign keys referencing the corresponding tables to ensure data consistency and integrity.",
  "gold_question": "The news publishing company needs to manage the submission, review, and publishing process of news articles. Each reporter can submit multiple articles, and each article needs to be reviewed by an editor. After passing the review, the article is published by a publisher. The system needs to record the submission time, review time, and publishing time of each article, as well as the information of the reporter, editor, and publisher.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0047.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0047\nCREATE TABLE `reporter` (\n  `reporter_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`reporter_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `news_article` (\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `publication_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `review_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `submission_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`article_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `editor` (\n  `editor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`editor_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `publisher` (\n  `publisher_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`publisher_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `article_reporter_table` (\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `reporter_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`article_id`, `reporter_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `article_reporter_table_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`article_id`) REFERENCES `news_article` (`article_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `article_reporter_table_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`reporter_id`) REFERENCES `reporter` (`reporter_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `article_editor_table` (\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `editor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`article_id`, `editor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `article_editor_table_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`article_id`) REFERENCES `news_article` (`article_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `article_editor_table_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`editor_id`) REFERENCES `editor` (`editor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `article_publisher_table` (\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `publisher_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`article_id`, `publisher_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `article_publisher_table_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`article_id`) REFERENCES `news_article` (`article_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `article_publisher_table_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`publisher_id`) REFERENCES `publisher` (`publisher_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
